Re: 14 Mosswold Crescent — rats in the kitchen.

Thank you for the updates on 1, 7 and 8 September. We have recorded that pest control removed its equipment on 7 September and that nobody attended on 8 September to fill the openings.

The landlord elected on 18 August to arrange this work directly. We have today written to him asking either for the contractor and completion date for the proofing work, or for his written authority for us to instruct our own pest-control contractor. We have asked him to reply by 5pm on Tuesday 16 September. If he does not, we will refer the case to our property manager. We cannot book a visit until one of those two things happens, so we are not giving you a date we cannot back.

In the meantime, to limit the problem:
- keep food (including pet food) in sealed containers and clear spillages and waste promptly;
- keep the area under the sink clear so any opening and any droppings stay visible;
- do not handle bait or traps left in place; wear gloves and wash hands after cleaning droppings;
- tell us straight away if you see gnawed cables or pipework, or smell burning or gas, if any rodent gets into a cupboard with electrics, or if anyone in the household is bitten or unwell — we will treat that as an emergency.

We note you prefer a phone call (event-017) and we will call you with the next update. Please let us know of any further sightings.
